    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. For q-18523, the base 1/6 gives exponential decay and the coefficient 2 gives intercept (0,2), matching option 0 and the solution's blue graph. For q-28973, a positive exponential with base between 0 and 1 has domain R, range (0,infinity), and decreases. The tangent slopes are 2(-2)-3=-7 and 10(1)+4=14; point-slope form gives the selected lines. Standard trigonometric and power derivatives give the four derivative/rate answers; sec²(pi)=1. The chain rule gives factors 3·6=18, 3·(-5)=-15, and 5·3=15. Permutations give 6, 52·51=2652, 7!=5040, and 5·4=20. Ashley's Thursday and Friday assignments are distinguishable, so there are 5·4=20 choices.",
